---
description: Log querying via txt2png pipeline
alwaysApply: true
globs: []
---

MANDATORY When query, tail >50 lines, searching logs, always pipe the output through
"<command> | <optional filters> | txt2png" and fetch 1st, last, middle PNG frames by
posted links. Inspect more frames, only if really needed. Never dump raw log text
directly into context. Do that for all logs related commands, also with grep/awk/sed
etc filters of system journal and logs, must-gather, sos-reports, an app stdout stream.
Prefer aggregating multiple commands outputs via files before piping it to txt2png.
If a command does not support piping (interactive pager, -f follow mode blocking),
use --no-pager or redirect to a temp file first. If a command output size cannot be
guessed (-o yaml/json) always aggregate multiple commands outputs to a file first.

NEVER use txt2png when:
- Reading or inspecting non-log files (source code, configs, YAML, JSON, manifests)
- Running commands that produce brief outputs, like ip, git, ls, cat of
  small files, helm, env, echo, pwd
- The expected output is under ~50 lines and there is no other steps/commands to aggregate its outputs
